<h2 class=3D"text-xl font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5">Part 1: Warm-up =
&amp; Introduction</h2>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Go=
od morning! I'm David Kim, Principal Engineer on the KYC team at Binance. I=
've been leading frontend architecture here for about 8 years, focusing on =
our identity verification systems that serve over 100 million users globall=
y. Today we'll dive deep into your React and JavaScript expertise, which is=
 absolutely critical for our high-scale, compliance-heavy environment. Coul=
d you start by walking me through your JavaScript journey and tell me about=
 the most challenging React application you've built?</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: Good=
 morning David! Thank you for having me. I'm Alex, and I've been immersed i=
n JavaScript for the past 7 years, with 5+ years specifically focused on Re=
act in production environments. My journey started with vanilla JavaScript =
and jQuery, but I quickly gravitated toward React when I realized its power=
 for building complex, stateful applications.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The most challenging React appli=
cation I've architected was a <strong>real-time cryptocurrency trading plat=
form</strong> similar to Binance's scope, serving about 2 million active tr=
aders. The complexity came from multiple fronts:</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Technical Challenges</st=
rong>:</p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Real-time data orchestr=
ation</strong>: Managing 50+ WebSocket connections simultaneously, handling=
 price feeds for 500+ trading pairs updating every 100ms</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>State complexity</stron=
g>: Coordinating user portfolios, order books, trade history, P&amp;L calcu=
lations, and risk management - all requiring <strong>sub-millisecond UI upd=
ates</strong></li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Performance constraints=
</strong>: Maintaining 60fps rendering while processing thousands of price =
updates per second</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Memory management</stro=
ng>: Preventing memory leaks during 12+ hour trading sessions</li>
</ul>
