<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The <strong>breakthrough moment<=
/strong> was implementing a <strong>virtualized state management system</st=
rong> where we only kept active trading pairs in memory and lazy-loaded his=
torical data. This reduced memory usage by 70% while maintaining instant re=
sponsiveness.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Business Impact</strong>=
: The platform handled <strong>$2.3 billion in daily trading volume</strong=
> with 99.99% uptime and average latency under 50ms for critical user inter=
actions.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Im=
pressive scale! I'm particularly interested in your real-time data handling=
. At Binance KYC, we face similar challenges with document verification sta=
tus updates, risk scoring changes, and compliance flag updates that need ne=
ar-instantaneous UI reflection. How do you approach the challenge of keepin=
g React components performant when dealing with high-frequency updates? Wha=
t patterns have you found most effective for preventing unnecessary re-rend=
ers?</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: <str=
ong>High-frequency updates with React performance</strong> is exactly where=
 many applications fail at scale. I've developed a <strong>multi-layered op=
timization strategy</strong> that I've refined across several high-traffic =
applications:</p>
